# General Coding Preferences
- Use 4 spaces for indentation
- Don't be lazy. Be thorough in your work
- Prefer trailing closures for better readability
- Avoid force unwrapping optionals; use optional binding or guard statements
- Keep functions short and focused on a single task
- When given a bug or told about something that is not working correctly, first reflect on 5-7 different possible sources of the problem, distill those down to 1-2 most likely sources, and then add logs to validate your assumptions before we move onto implementing the actual code fix
- Sometimes error messages/linter errors don't go away until I clean the build; it doesn't mean you have to keep trying to "fix" a problem that already may have been fixed
- Please keep in mind that I don't run projects in the simulator through XCode; I use sweetpad right on here. Don't try to launch XCode for me.
- Avoid redeclaring methods or properties with the same name across protocols and classes
- Be careful with extensions that reference their own properties or methods
- When fixing compiler errors, a clean build is often necessary to clear any stale artifacts
- When doing a complete rebuild/rewrite of something, obviously keep the *exact* same styling as before in your new implementation. Not a thing must look different. Don't be lazy.



